<edge source="middle_east_maritime_con::chokepoint_transit_flow" target="china_eu_industrial_riva::import_market_share" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained reductions in commercial transit through a chokepoint raise delivery delays and freight costs for imported vehicles, causing importers to cut volumes and buyers to shift toward locally produced models, reducing import market share.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">middle_east_maritime_con</data>
  <data key="d39">china_eu_industrial_riva</data>
</edge>
<edge source="middle_east_maritime_con::chokepoint_transit_flow" target="china_eu_industrial_riva::capital_flow_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved and reliable chokepoint transit (an increase in flow) lowers the business case for nearshoring and capacity building in the consuming region, thereby reducing new cross‑border investment into local vehicle manufacturing and supply‑chain assets.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">middle_east_maritime_con</data>
  <data key="d39">china_eu_industrial_riva</data>
</edge>
<edge source="middle_east_maritime_con::chokepoint_transit_flow" target="russia_ukraine_war::fuel_reroute_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A slowdown or closure that reduces transit flow through a chokepoint forces carriers to divert cargo onto alternative (often longer) routes, increasing the rate at which fuel shipments are rerouted.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">middle_east_maritime_con</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
