  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher crude export flows (i.e., stable/often lower energy/shipping costs) reduce pressure on manufacturers to shorten supply chains, so increases in crude export flow tend to slow the pace at which firms raise local content and domestic sourcing.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
